From a3e7fedc59027ea1879c121813217d63261ed911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: azrialwork <azrial.work@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:17:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): add native android (Termux/Bionic) build target
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New target linux-arm64-android compiles against Bun's official android runtime, producing a PIE binary for /system/bin/linker64. The parcel-watcher and PTY bindings use their designed fallbacks (no android builds exist upstream).

OpenTUI publishes no android asset, so the build embeds a prepared asset tree: the linux-arm64-musl render library — which needs only libc.so, Bionic's own SONAME — plus a small compat shim (script/bionic-compat.c) covering the three symbols Bionic lacks and disabling heap pointer tagging, which Bun's FFI cannot represent. patchelf adds libm.so and the shim as NEEDED entries with an $ORIGIN rpath. A build-time audit fails if the render library's imports drift from script/opentui-musl-undefined.txt. At startup the CLI extracts the tree to its cache and re-execs once with OTUI_ASSET_ROOT set (the renderer reads an environment fixed at process start). A patchedDependencies entry maps @opentui/core's asset descriptor for android to the musl asset.
